==Western Apache==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ath-pro|apw}} {{m|ath-pro|*-ǯəγe·ʔ}}. Cognates: Navajo ''-jaa’'', Chiricahua ''-jaa'', Jicarilla ''-jaa'', Plains Apache ''-jaghe''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[d͡ʒàː]|lang=apw}}

===Noun===
'''-jaa''' (''[[inalienable]]'', e.g., '''shijaa''' "my ear", '''bijaa''' "her/his/their ear")

# [[ear]], outer ear

====Usage notes====
The form '''-jaa''' occurs in the San Carlos varieties; '''-jaa’''' occurs in White Mountain and Dilzhe’eh ([[Tonto]]).

